capability font/hinting  the instructions of a font run to fit its glyphs to a pixel grid
  heroes  refused: the outlines are read as the font draws them at its own scale; running `fpgm`, `prep` and the glyph programs is a rasteriser's work, and an interpreter of TrueType's instruction set is a program of its own which nothing in this package's callers asks for
  go      font.HintingNone, font.HintingVertical, font.HintingFull
  rust    -
  python  fontTools.ttLib.tables.ttProgram
  note    the programs are kept in a subset, so a reader that runs them still can

dropped
  go      sfnt.Buffer (re-usable buffers: Heroes values are copies), sfnt.ErrNotFound and sfnt.ErrColoredGlyph as variables (the codes `not_found` and `unsupported` are their answers), the `font.Face` interface (Heroes has no interface), font.Drawer's Dst, Src, Face and Dot fields (drawing)
  rust    Fixed, LazyArray16, LazyArray32, LazyArrayIter16, LazyArrayIter32, PointF, GlyphId, Face::from_raw_tables, Face::raw_face, Face::height, RawFaceTables, FromData, CFFError, Language, PlatformId, loca::Table, head::IndexToLocationFormat (zero-copy plumbing and the integer types of the crate's own representation, which `i64` and `f64` are)
  python  fontTools.ttLib.ttFont.TTFont.save, saveXML, importXML, ensureDecompiled, isLoaded, close, reorderGlyphs, setGlyphOrder and fontTools.ttLib's SFNTWriter, newTable, registerCustomTableClass, unregisterCustomTableClass, getTableClass, getCustomTableClass, getTableModule, getClassTag, getSearchRange, maxPowerOfTwo, sortedTagList, reorderFontTables, identifierToTag, tagToIdentifier, tagToXML, xmlToTag, tostr, byteord, debugmsg, Config, AbstractConfig, OPTIONS, OPTIMIZE_FONT_SPEED, TTFTableOrder, OTFTableOrder, beyond64k, ttVisitor, xmlWriter (a font compiler's and editor's own plumbing: writing a font from tables, its XML form and the library's configuration), fontTools.pens modules not named above (areaPen, cairoPen, cocoaPen, cu2quPen, explicitClosingLinePen, filterPen, freetypePen, hashPointPen, momentsPen, perimeterPen, pointInsidePen, pointPen, qtPen, qu2cuPen, quartzPen, reportLabPen, reverseContourPen, roundingPen, statisticsPen, svgPathPen, teePen, transformPen, wxPen: drawing targets and outline arithmetic, which a path's consumer does), fontTools.subset's options, visitors and layout pruning (NameRecordVisitor, NullPen, Counter, Timer, closure_lookups, collect_features, collect_lookups, intersect, intersect_class, intersect_glyphs, is_hinting, mirrored, neuter_lookups, parse_gids, parse_glyphs, parse_unicodes, prune_features, prune_hints, prune_lookups, prune_post_subset, prune_pre_subset, remap, remapComponentsFast, remap_duplicate_features, remove_hints, remove_redundant_langsys, retain_empty_scripts, subset, subset_feature_tags, subset_features, makeName, makeOutputFileName, maxCtxFont, may_have_non_1to1, multiVarStore, NAME_IDS_TO_OBFUSCATE, USE_HARFBUZZ_REPACKER: the layout tables are not carried)
